  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222931_FY24 #21_UNICEF_South Sudan - Health Sector Transformation Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Vision (WV) proposes an approach that will be led by the State Ministry of Health and County Health Department (CHD) anchored on improving access to life-saving primary, secondary and community health services to the most vulnerable women and children hence reducing the child and maternal morbidity and mortality rates in Maban, Renk and Melut counties. WV will align the above programming to the below outputs as set out for this CFEI: 
 
 Output 1.1 Frontline health and community workers demonstrate improved capacity to provide flexible, integrated services for the management of common childhood illnesses to young children in targeted emergency and non-emergency settings. 
 
 Output 1.2 Frontline health and community workers demonstrate improved capacity to provide quality, essential maternal and neonatal care to pregnant women and adolescent girls and their babies, in emergency and non-emergency settings. 
 
 Output 1.3 Government and other partners demonstrate improved capacity to deliver routine and supplementary immunization and respond to disease outbreaks.</narrative>
  </description>
